# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Introduction to symmetric key cryptography {#introduction-to-symmetric-key-"
"cryptography}"
msgstr ""
"مقدمة في تشفير المفتاح المتماثل {#introduction-to-symmetric-key-"
"cryptography}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Symmetric key cryptography (SKC)* is the oldest and most intuitive form of "
"cryptography. With SKC, confidential information is secured through "
"symmetric key encryption (SKE), that is, by using a <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"The same key is used for both encryption and decryption of "
"data. In this method, the sender and receiver share a secret key that is "
"used to transform the plaintext (original data) into ciphertext (encrypted "
"data) and vice versa.\">*single secret key*</DefinitionTooltip> for both "
"encryption and decryption.\n"
msgstr ""
"*تشفير المفتاح المتماثل (SKC)* هو أقدم أشكال التشفير وأكثرها بديهية. في SKC،"
" تُؤمَّن المعلومات السرية عبر تشفير المفتاح المتماثل (SKE)، أي باستخدام "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The same key is used for both encryption and"
" decryption of data. In this method, the sender and receiver share a secret "
"key that is used to transform the plaintext (original data) into ciphertext "
"(encrypted data) and vice versa.\">*مفتاح سري واحد*</DefinitionTooltip> "
"لعمليتَي التشفير وفك التشفير معًا.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"SKC involves:\n"
"- An encryption function that converts a given plain text instance to <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The result of applying an encryption algorithm to the plaintext using a specific encryption key; one needs the correct decryption key to transform ciphertext back to plaintext.\">ciphertext</DefinitionTooltip> while utilizing a secret key\n"
"- A decryption function that inverts the operation by converting the ciphertext back to plain text using the same secret key\n"
msgstr ""
"يشمل SKC:\n"
"- دالة تشفير تحوّل نصًّا عاديًّا معيّنًا إلى <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The result of applying an encryption algorithm to the plaintext using a specific encryption key; one needs the correct decryption key to transform ciphertext back to plaintext.\">ciphertext</DefinitionTooltip> مع استخدام مفتاح سري\n"
"- دالة فك تشفير تعكس العملية بتحويل ciphertext مجددًا إلى نص عادي باستخدام المفتاح السري ذاته\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Plain text can mean any kind of unencrypted data such as natural language "
"text or binary code whose information content is in principle directly "
"accessible, while <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The result of applying an "
"encryption algorithm to the plaintext using a specific encryption key; one "
"needs the correct decryption key to transform ciphertext back to "
"plaintext.\">ciphertext</DefinitionTooltip> refers to encrypted data whose "
"information content is intended to be inaccessible prior to decryption.\n"
msgstr ""
"النص العادي يمكن أن يكون أي نوع من البيانات غير المشفّرة كالنص البشري "
"الطبيعي أو الشفرة الثنائية التي يمكن الوصول إلى محتواها المعلوماتي مبدئيًّا،"
" بينما يشير <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The result of applying an "
"encryption algorithm to the plaintext using a specific encryption key; one "
"needs the correct decryption key to transform ciphertext back to "
"plaintext.\">ciphertext</DefinitionTooltip> إلى البيانات المشفّرة التي يُقصد"
" ألّا يكون محتواها متاحًا قبل فك التشفير.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An algorithm that describes the encryption and decryption operations using a"
" shared secret key is also called a symmetric cipher.\n"
msgstr ""
"الخوارزمية التي تصف عمليتَي التشفير وفك التشفير باستخدام مفتاح سري مشترك "
"تُسمّى أيضًا symmetric cipher.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Fig 1: Symmetric key encryption of a given plaintext to ciphertext and "
"decryption back to plaintext using the same "
"key.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-cryptography/symmetric-key-"
"cryptography/skc.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![الشكل 1: تشفير المفتاح المتماثل لنص عادي معطى إلى ciphertext وفك تشفيره "
"مجددًا إلى النص العادي باستخدام المفتاح "
"ذاته.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-cryptography/symmetric-key-"
"cryptography/skc.svg)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Figure 1. Symmetric key encryption of a given plain text to ciphertext and "
"decryption back to plain text using the same key.*\n"
msgstr ""
"*الشكل 1. تشفير المفتاح المتماثل لنص عادي معطى إلى ciphertext وفك تشفيره "
"مجددًا إلى النص العادي باستخدام المفتاح ذاته.*\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Properties of symmetric key cryptosystems {#properties-of-symmetric-key-"
"cryptosystems}"
msgstr ""
"خصائص أنظمة تشفير المفتاح المتماثل {#properties-of-symmetric-key-"
"cryptosystems}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A symmetric key cryptosystem should ensure the following properties to "
"secure messages-both statically stored data and/or communications over some "
"transmission channel:\n"
msgstr ""
"يجب أن يضمن نظام تشفير المفتاح المتماثل الخصائص التالية لتأمين الرسائل — "
"سواء أكانت بيانات مخزّنة ساكنة أم اتصالات عبر قناة إرسال ما:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Confidentiality:** Refers to the property that the information content of "
"encrypted messages is protected from unauthorized access.\n"
msgstr ""
"**السرية:** تشير إلى خاصية حماية محتوى الرسائل المشفّرة من الوصول غير "
"المصرّح به.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Integrity:** Refers to the property that any tampering of encrypted "
"messages during storage or transmission can be detected.\n"
msgstr ""
"**النزاهة:** تشير إلى خاصية إمكانية اكتشاف أي تلاعب بالرسائل المشفّرة أثناء "
"التخزين أو الإرسال.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Authenticity:**  Refers to the property that the receiver of a message can"
" verify the identity of the sender and detect impersonation by an "
"unauthorized party.\n"
msgstr ""
"**الأصالة:** تشير إلى خاصية تمكين مستلم الرسالة من التحقق من هوية المرسل "
"واكتشاف انتحال الشخصية من قِبَل طرف غير مصرّح له.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Furthermore, these properties should be realized in a setting where the "
"algorithms or ciphers used for encryption and decryption may be public and "
"where access to the information content of encrypted messages is controlled "
"exclusively through access to the secret key.\n"
msgstr ""
"علاوة على ذلك، يجب تحقيق هذه الخصائص في بيئة قد تكون فيها الخوارزميات أو "
"الأصفار المستخدمة للتشفير وفك التشفير عامّة، وحيث يُتحكَّم في الوصول إلى "
"محتوى الرسائل المشفّرة حصرًا عبر الوصول إلى المفتاح السري.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Implementing a secure symmetric key cryptosystem therefore involves two main"
" tasks:\n"
msgstr "لذا فإن تطبيق نظام تشفير مفتاح متماثل آمن يتضمّن مهمتين رئيسيتين:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Employing a robust symmetric key encryption algorithm resistant to "
"cryptographic attacks.\n"
msgstr "استخدام خوارزمية تشفير مفتاح متماثل قوية مقاومة للهجمات التشفيرية.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Ensuring confidentiality in the distribution and management of secret "
"keys.\n"
msgstr "ضمان سرية توزيع المفاتيح السرية وإدارتها.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this lesson, we will discuss aspects related to the first task, which "
"forms the primary concern of SKC technology. The second task, however, needs"
" solutions that fall outside of SKC itself and will be introduced later.\n"
msgstr ""
"في هذا الدرس سنناقش الجوانب المتعلقة بالمهمة الأولى التي تشكّل الاهتمام "
"الرئيسي لتقنية SKC. أما المهمة الثانية فتحتاج إلى حلول تقع خارج نطاق SKC "
"ذاتها وسيتم تقديمها لاحقًا.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Illustration of symmetric key encryption using python {#illustration-of-"
"symmetric-key-encryption-using-python}"
msgstr ""
"توضيح تشفير المفتاح المتماثل باستخدام Python {#illustration-of-symmetric-"
"key-encryption-using-python}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We show a simple example of the encrypt and decrypt operations using the classical <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The Caesar shift cipher is a simple encryption scheme use since Roman times, or before. Each letter is substituted by one other, shifted by a number of letters. It's a type of monoalphabetic substitution cipher.\">Caesar shift cipher</DefinitionTooltip> and the modern <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Advanced Encryption Standard is a specification for encryption of data, and was established by NIST in 2001. It was originated from the Rijndael ciphers developed by Joan Daemen and Vincent Rijmen, two Belgium cryptographers. It is defined in FIBS 197 & ISO/IEC 18033-3.\">Advanced Encryption System</DefinitionTooltip> (AES), which has been the standard for symmetric key encryption since 2001.\n"
"First we set up some Python libraries that provide the needed symmetric key encryption ciphers, and then define the plain text we wish to encrypt.\n"
msgstr ""
"سنعرض مثالًا بسيطًا لعمليتَي التشفير وفك التشفير باستخدام <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The Caesar shift cipher is a simple encryption scheme use since Roman times, or before. Each letter is substituted by one other, shifted by a number of letters. It's a type of monoalphabetic substitution cipher.\">Caesar shift cipher</DefinitionTooltip> الكلاسيكي ونظام <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Advanced Encryption Standard is a specification for encryption of data, and was established by NIST in 2001. It was originated from the Rijndael ciphers developed by Joan Daemen and Vincent Rijmen, two Belgium cryptographers. It is defined in FIBS 197 & ISO/IEC 18033-3.\">Advanced Encryption System</DefinitionTooltip> (AES) الحديث الذي أصبح معيار تشفير المفتاح المتماثل منذ عام 2001.\n"
"أولًا سنضبط بعض مكتبات Python التي توفّر أصفار تشفير المفتاح المتماثل المطلوبة، ثم نحدّد النص العادي الذي نريد تشفيره.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will see how to encrypt and decrypt it using two different symmetric key "
"encryption methods:\n"
msgstr ""
"سنرى كيفية تشفيره وفك تشفيره باستخدام طريقتين مختلفتين لتشفير المفتاح "
"المتماثل:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The classic [Caesar shift "
"cipher](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Caesar_cipher&oldid=1151194063)\n"
msgstr ""
"الكلاسيكي [Caesar shift "
"cipher](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Caesar_cipher&oldid=1151194063)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The modern [Advanced Encryption "
"Standard](https://www.nist.gov/publications/development-advanced-encryption-"
"standard) AES-256 protocol\n"
msgstr ""
"البروتوكول الحديث [Advanced Encryption "
"Standard](https://www.nist.gov/publications/development-advanced-encryption-"
"standard) AES-256\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Caesar shift cipher: {#caesar-shift-cipher}"
msgstr "Caesar shift cipher: {#caesar-shift-cipher}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Caesar shift encryption involves defining\n"
" - An alphabet of possible characters to encode\n"
" - A *shift value* which can be between 0 (unencrypted) and the length of the alphabet. We consider this the *key*.\n"
msgstr ""
"يتضمّن تشفير Caesar shift تحديد:\n"
" - أبجدية الأحرف الممكنة للترميز\n"
" - *قيمة الإزاحة* التي يمكن أن تتراوح بين 0 (بدون تشفير) وطول الأبجدية. نعتبر هذه هي *المفتاح*.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is known as a *monoalphabetic substitution cipher* since each letter of "
"the plain text is substituted with another in the ciphertext.\n"
msgstr ""
"يُعرف بأنه *monoalphabetic substitution cipher* لأن كل حرف من النص العادي "
"يُستبدل بحرف آخر في ciphertext.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "In this example we will use lowercase letters of the alphabet.\n"
msgstr "في هذا المثال سنستخدم الأحرف الصغيرة من الأبجدية.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Let's start by setting things up.\n"
msgstr "لنبدأ بإعداد الأمور.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Encrypt the plain text to get ciphertext for the Caesar cipher.\n"
msgstr "شفّر النص العادي للحصول على النص المشفّر باستخدام تشفير Caesar.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Decrypt the ciphertext back to the original plain text using the same key "
"used for encryption.\n"
msgstr ""
"فكّ تشفير النص المشفّر للرجوع إلى النص العادي الأصلي باستخدام نفس المفتاح "
"المستخدم في التشفير.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Advanced encryption standard (AES) cipher {#advanced-encryption-standard-"
"aes-cipher}"
msgstr ""
"تشفير المعيار المتقدم (AES) {#advanced-encryption-standard-aes-cipher}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We now encrypt the plain text using AES, a popular symmetric key encryption "
"algorithm.\n"
msgstr ""
"هنا نشفّر النص العادي باستخدام AES، وهو خوارزمية تشفير بالمفتاح المتماثل "
"شائعة الاستخدام.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We start by creating the key, in this case, a random 16-letter string.\n"
msgstr "نبدأ بإنشاء المفتاح، وفي هذه الحالة سيكون سلسلة عشوائية من 16 حرفًا.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"AES supports multiple operating modes and requires we specify which to "
"use.\n"
msgstr "يدعم AES عدة أنماط تشغيل وعلينا تحديد النمط الذي نريد استخدامه.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We choose the *Cipher Block Chaining* (CBC) mode provided by the `modes.CBC`"
" class of the `cryptography` library. The CBC mode of AES uses randomness "
"for additional security. This requires specifying a random *Initialization "
"Vector* (IV), also called a <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Number used "
"once.\">*nonce*</DefinitionTooltip>. We will use a random string for this as"
" well, just like we did for the key.\n"
msgstr ""
"نختار نمط *Cipher Block Chaining* (CBC) المتوفر في الكلاس `modes.CBC` من "
"مكتبة `cryptography`. يستخدم نمط CBC في AES عشوائية لتعزيز الأمان، وهذا "
"يستلزم تحديد *Initialization Vector* (IV) عشوائي، يُعرف أيضًا بـ "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Number used "
"once.\">*nonce*</DefinitionTooltip>. سنستخدم سلسلة عشوائية لهذا الغرض أيضًا،"
" تمامًا كما فعلنا مع المفتاح.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can now instantiate an AES cipher on behalf of the sender of the secret "
"message. Note that the initialization vector is passed to the `modes.CBC` "
"class to set up the CBC mode of operation.\n"
msgstr ""
"يمكننا الآن إنشاء تشفير AES نيابةً عن مُرسِل الرسالة السرية. لاحظ أن "
"initialization vector يُمرَّر إلى الكلاس `modes.CBC` لإعداد نمط تشغيل CBC.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We will then encrypt the plain text to send.\n"
msgstr "ثم نشفّر النص العادي لإرساله.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To decrypt it, let us instantiate an AES cipher on behalf of the receiver. "
"Note that the intended receiver has access to both the secret key and the "
"initialization vector, but the latter is not required to be secret.\n"
msgstr ""
"لفكّ التشفير، لنُنشئ تشفير AES نيابةً عن المستقبِل. لاحظ أن المستقبِل "
"المقصود لديه حق الوصول إلى المفتاح السري وإلى initialization vector، لكن "
"الأخير لا يشترط أن يكون سريًا.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Applications of symmetric key cryptography {#applications-of-symmetric-key-"
"cryptography}"
msgstr ""
"تطبيقات التشفير بالمفتاح المتماثل {#applications-of-symmetric-key-"
"cryptography}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"While classical ciphers such as the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The "
"Caesar shift cipher is a simple encryption scheme use since Roman times, or "
"before. Each letter is substituted by one other, shifted by a number of "
"letters. It's a type of monoalphabetic substitution cipher.\">Caesar "
"cipher</DefinitionTooltip> fell out of use a long time ago, modern symmetric"
" cryptosystems such as AES are [deployed in a wide range of "
"applications](https://books.google.com/books?id=01vfjgEACAAJ), including:\n"
msgstr ""
"بينما خرجت الشفرات الكلاسيكية من الاستخدام منذ زمن بعيد، مثل "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The Caesar shift cipher is a simple "
"encryption scheme use since Roman times, or before. Each letter is "
"substituted by one other, shifted by a number of letters. It's a type of "
"monoalphabetic substitution cipher.\">تشفير Caesar</DefinitionTooltip>، فإن "
"أنظمة التشفير المتماثل الحديثة مثل AES [تُستخدم في مجموعة واسعة من "
"التطبيقات](https://books.google.com/books?id=01vfjgEACAAJ)، منها:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Data encryption and decryption:** SKC is widely used to protect sensitive "
"data, whether statically stored on a device or transmitted over a network. "
"Examples include protecting user credentials, encrypting email messages, and"
" securing financial transactions, among others.\n"
msgstr ""
"**تشفير البيانات وفكّ تشفيرها:** يُستخدم SKC على نطاق واسع لحماية البيانات "
"الحساسة، سواء كانت مخزّنة على جهاز أو مُرسَلة عبر الشبكة. تشمل الأمثلة حماية"
" بيانات اعتماد المستخدمين، وتشفير رسائل البريد الإلكتروني، وتأمين المعاملات "
"المالية وغير ذلك.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Secure communication:** Common communication protocols such as "
"SSL/[TLS](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Transport_Layer_Security&oldid=1155601531)"
" use a combination of symmetric and asymmetric key encryption to ensure the "
"confidentiality and integrity of data exchanged between two parties. These "
"messages are encrypted and decrypted using symmetric key encryption which "
"uses a shared key. The key used in symmetric key encryption is securely "
"exchanged using asymmetric key encryption which uses a public-private key "
"pair. Symmetric key encryption is much faster and hence can be used for "
"encryption of messages of large size.\n"
msgstr ""
"**الاتصالات الآمنة:** تستخدم بروتوكولات الاتصال الشائعة مثل "
"SSL/[TLS](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Transport_Layer_Security&oldid=1155601531)"
" مزيجًا من تشفير المفتاح المتماثل وغير المتماثل لضمان سرية البيانات "
"المتبادلة بين طرفين وسلامتها. تُشفَّر هذه الرسائل وتُفكَّك باستخدام تشفير "
"المفتاح المتماثل الذي يعتمد على مفتاح مشترك. ويُتبادَل المفتاح المستخدم في "
"التشفير المتماثل بأمان عبر تشفير المفتاح غير المتماثل الذي يعتمد على زوج "
"مفاتيح عامة-خاصة. التشفير بالمفتاح المتماثل أسرع بكثير، ومن ثَمّ يمكن "
"استخدامه لتشفير رسائل ضخمة الحجم.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Authenticity verification:** In some settings, SKC is employed through "
"techniques like [message authentication "
"codes](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Message_authentication_code&oldid=1151014755)"
" (MACs) and keyed-hash MACs (HMAC) to verify the <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Authenticity is the proof that a message is from the source it "
"claims to be from.\">authenticity</DefinitionTooltip> and <DefinitionTooltip"
" definition=\"Integrity is maintained when a message is protected against "
"unauthorized change.\">integrity</DefinitionTooltip> of messages, ensuring "
"tamper-resistant communication.\n"
msgstr ""
"**التحقق من الأصالة:** في بعض السياقات، يُستخدم SKC عبر تقنيات مثل [رموز "
"مصادقة "
"الرسائل](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Message_authentication_code&oldid=1151014755)"
" (MACs) ورموز HMAC للتحقق من <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Authenticity is"
" the proof that a message is from the source it claims to be "
"from.\">أصالة</DefinitionTooltip> الرسائل و<DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Integrity is maintained when a message is protected against "
"unauthorized change.\">سلامتها</DefinitionTooltip>، وضمان اتصالات مقاومة "
"للتلاعب.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**File and disk encryption:** Full-disk encryption software and file "
"encryption tools employ SKC to protect sensitive data stored on hard disks "
"or portable storage devices.\n"
msgstr ""
"**تشفير الملفات والأقراص:** تعتمد برامج تشفير القرص الكامل وأدوات تشفير "
"الملفات على SKC لحماية البيانات الحساسة المخزّنة على الأقراص الصلبة أو أجهزة"
" التخزين المحمولة.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Virtual private networks:** "
"[VPN](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Virtual_private_network&oldid=1154342615)"
" technologies, which aim to provide confidential communication channels free"
" from eavesdropping, can use symmetric or asymmetric key encryption to "
"connect remote users as well as corporate networks.\n"
msgstr ""
"**الشبكات الافتراضية الخاصة:** تهدف تقنيات "
"[VPN](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Virtual_private_network&oldid=1154342615)"
" إلى توفير قنوات اتصال سرية بعيدة عن التنصت، ويمكنها استخدام تشفير المفتاح "
"المتماثل أو غير المتماثل لربط المستخدمين عن بُعد وكذلك شبكات الشركات.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The diverse array of applications in which SKC is deployed in turn require "
"that symmetric cryptosystems satisfy a certain set of criteria.\n"
msgstr ""
"التنوع الكبير في التطبيقات التي يُستخدم فيها SKC يستلزم بدوره أن تستوفي "
"أنظمة التشفير المتماثل مجموعة من المعايير المحددة.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Principles of symmetric key encryption {#principles-of-symmetric-key-"
"encryption}"
msgstr ""
"مبادئ التشفير بالمفتاح المتماثل {#principles-of-symmetric-key-encryption}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this section, we will discuss some of the basic [principles underlying "
"the security of symmetric key encryption "
"algorithms](https://doi.org/10.1080/07468342.1987.11973000).\n"
msgstr ""
"في هذا القسم، سنناقش بعض [المبادئ الأساسية التي يقوم عليها أمان خوارزميات "
"التشفير بالمفتاح "
"المتماثل](https://doi.org/10.1080/07468342.1987.11973000).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Resistance to brute force attack:** The most basic requirement for the "
"security of an encryption cipher is that the key space size — in other "
"words, the number of possible distinct keys from which someone using the "
"algorithm could have chosen — is very large.\n"
msgstr ""
"**المقاومة ضد هجمات القوة الغاشمة:** المتطلب الأساسي لأمان أي شفرة تشفير هو "
"أن يكون حجم فضاء المفاتيح — أي عدد المفاتيح المتميزة الممكنة التي كان بإمكان"
" مستخدم الخوارزمية الاختيار منها — كبيرًا جدًا.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Resistance to cryptanalytic attack:** The second basic requirement for a "
"cipher, symmetric or otherwise, is that it can generate ciphertexts that are"
" informationally <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The property of the "
"encrypted data being extremely difficult, if not practically impossible, to "
"understand or decipher without the correct decryption "
"key.\">inscrutable</DefinitionTooltip>. To this end, a necessary but not "
"sufficient condition from an information theory perspective is that "
"[ciphertexts should be characterized by high "
"entropy](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Entropy_(information_theory)&oldid=1154931420),"
" making them indistinguishable from random text with no discernible patterns"
" or correlations. This way, an attacker can gain no information about the "
"plain text or secret key by trying to analyze the ciphertext using frequency"
" analysis or other statistical techniques.\n"
msgstr ""
"**المقاومة ضد هجمات التحليل التشفيري:** المتطلب الأساسي الثاني لأي شفرة، "
"متماثلة أو غيرها، هو قدرتها على توليد نصوص مشفّرة <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"The property of the encrypted data being extremely difficult, "
"if not practically impossible, to understand or decipher without the correct"
" decryption key.\">يصعب استيعابها</DefinitionTooltip> من الناحية "
"المعلوماتية. لتحقيق هذا، شرط ضروري لكنه غير كافٍ من منظور نظرية المعلومات هو"
" أن [تتميز النصوص المشفّرة بانتروبيا "
"عالية](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Entropy_(information_theory)&oldid=1154931420)،"
" مما يجعلها لا تختلف عن النص العشوائي بدون أنماط أو ارتباطات واضحة. بهذه "
"الطريقة، لا يستطيع المهاجم الحصول على أي معلومات عن النص العادي أو المفتاح "
"السري من خلال محاولة تحليل النص المشفّر باستخدام تحليل التردد أو غيره من "
"التقنيات الإحصائية.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Resistance to general forms of cryptanalytic attacks sufficient to ensure "
"[semantic "
"security](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Semantic_security&oldid=1133491450)"
" is formalized via the notion of "
"[*indistinguishability*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Ciphertext_indistinguishability&oldid=1130147047)."
" While there are several variants of indistinguishability with distinct "
"requirements, a symmetric cryptosystem is considered to be semantically "
"secure if it satisfies the criterion of [*Indistinguishability under Chosen "
"Plain Text "
"Attack*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Ciphertext_indistinguishability&oldid=1130147047)"
" (IND-CPA). This means that an attacker cannot distinguish between the "
"encryptions of two different messages even if allowed to send multiple plain"
" texts of their choosing to the algorithm and view the corresponding "
"ciphertexts.\n"
msgstr ""
"تتجسّد المقاومة ضد الأشكال العامة لهجمات التحليل التشفيري الكافية لضمان "
"[الأمان "
"الدلالي](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Semantic_security&oldid=1133491450)"
" رسميًا عبر مفهوم [*عدم "
"التمييز*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Ciphertext_indistinguishability&oldid=1130147047)."
" وعلى الرغم من وجود عدة أشكال لعدم التمييز بمتطلبات مختلفة، يُعدّ نظام "
"التشفير المتماثل آمنًا دلاليًا إذا استوفى معيار [*عدم التمييز في ظل هجوم "
"النص العادي "
"المختار*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Ciphertext_indistinguishability&oldid=1130147047)"
" (IND-CPA). يعني هذا أن المهاجم لا يستطيع التمييز بين تشفيري رسالتين "
"مختلفتين حتى لو سُمح له بإرسال نصوص عادية متعددة من اختياره إلى الخوارزمية "
"ومشاهدة النصوص المشفّرة المقابلة.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As we will consider later, IND-CPA typically requires the use of randomness "
"to ensure that each time a given plain text is encrypted with a given secret"
" key, the resulting ciphertext is unpredictably different for each "
"encryption.\n"
msgstr ""
"كما سنرى لاحقًا، يستلزم IND-CPA عادةً استخدام العشوائية لضمان أن كل مرة "
"يُشفَّر فيها نص عادي معين بمفتاح سري معين، يكون النص المشفّر الناتج مختلفًا "
"بشكل غير متوقع في كل عملية تشفير.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Failure modes of classical ciphers:** Before the advent of modern "
"cryptography in the 1970s, most classical ciphers in practical use failed to"
" satisfy one or both above requirements. For instance, early substitution "
"ciphers such as the monoalphabetic [Caesar shift "
"cipher](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Caesar_cipher&oldid=1151194063)"
" were characterized by both a small key space size (see <a href=\"#Table "
"1\">Table 1</a>) and low entropy ciphertext, making them insecure against a "
"variety of cryptanalytic attacks such as brute force attacks, frequency "
"analysis, and known-plain-text (KPT) attacks.\n"
msgstr ""
"**أوجه قصور الشفرات الكلاسيكية:** قبل ظهور التشفير الحديث في سبعينيات القرن "
"الماضي، كانت معظم الشفرات الكلاسيكية المستخدمة عمليًا تفشل في استيفاء أحد "
"هذين المتطلبين أو كليهما. على سبيل المثال، اتسمت شفرات الاستبدال المبكرة "
"كـ[تشفير Caesar الأحادي "
"الأبجدية](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Caesar_cipher&oldid=1151194063)"
" بصغر حجم فضاء المفاتيح (انظر <a href=\"#Table 1\">الجدول 1</a>) وانخفاض "
"انتروبيا النص المشفّر، مما جعلها غير آمنة أمام مجموعة متنوعة من هجمات "
"التحليل التشفيري كهجمات القوة الغاشمة وتحليل التردد وهجمات النص العادي "
"المعروف (KPT).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Subsequent polyalphabetic substitution ciphers such as the [Vigenère "
"cipher](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Vigen%C3%A8re_cipher&oldid=1155012941)"
" and the [Enigma machine "
"cipher](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Enigma_machine&oldid=1154440070)"
" featured effectively large key space sizes, making them resistant to brute "
"force attacks, but they were susceptible to frequency analysis and KPT "
"attacks, respectively. Similarly to substitution ciphers, [classic "
"transposition "
"ciphers](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Transposition_cipher&oldid=1151499771),"
" which rearrange letters in a message instead of substituting them, are also"
" compromised by a variety of attacks such as anagramming, statistical "
"analysis, brute force, and KPT attacks, among others.\n"
msgstr ""
"جاءت بعدها شفرات الاستبدال متعددة الأبجديات مثل [تشفير "
"Vigenère](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Vigen%C3%A8re_cipher&oldid=1155012941)"
" و[تشفير آلة "
"Enigma](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Enigma_machine&oldid=1154440070)"
" بفضاء مفاتيح كبير فعليًا يجعلها مقاومة لهجمات القوة الغاشمة، لكنها كانت "
"عرضة لتحليل التردد وهجمات KPT على التوالي. وعلى غرار شفرات الاستبدال، فإن "
"[شفرات التبديل "
"الكلاسيكية](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Transposition_cipher&oldid=1151499771)"
" التي تُعيد ترتيب الحروف في الرسالة بدلًا من استبدالها، تتعرض هي الأخرى "
"لأنواع متعددة من الهجمات كالتحريف الأنغرامي والتحليل الإحصائي والقوة الغاشمة"
" وهجمات KPT وغيرها.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Theoretically, a polyalphabetic substitution cipher known as the [one-time "
"pad](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=One-"
"time_pad&oldid=1155039884) (OTP) is known to be cryptographically secure. An"
" OTP features a secret key that should be (1) composed of randomly chosen "
"letters or bits, (2) at least as long as the original plain text, and (3) "
"used only once. An OTP is impractical for actual applications because if the"
" secret key — which is required to be as long as the plain text and can be "
"used only once — could be shared securely, then so could the original plain "
"text. The OTP instead illustrates the utility of randomness in generating "
"secure ciphertexts.\n"
msgstr ""
"من الناحية النظرية، تشفير الاستبدال متعدد الأبجديات المعروف بـ[one-time "
"pad](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=One-"
"time_pad&oldid=1155039884) (OTP) آمن تشفيريًا. يتميز OTP بمفتاح سري ينبغي أن"
" يكون: (1) مكوّنًا من حروف أو بتات مختارة عشوائيًا، (2) بطول لا يقل عن النص "
"العادي الأصلي، (3) مستخدمًا مرة واحدة فقط. لكن OTP غير عملي للتطبيقات "
"الفعلية لأنه لو أمكن تبادل المفتاح السري — الذي يجب أن يكون بطول النص العادي"
" ولا يُستخدم إلا مرة — بأمان، لأمكن كذلك تبادل النص العادي الأصلي. يبرز OTP "
"في المقابل قيمة العشوائية في توليد نصوص مشفّرة آمنة.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An attacker trying to implement a brute force search through the key space "
"to find a key that decrypts the message has to perform a number of "
"operations proportional to the key space size.\n"
msgstr ""
"على المهاجم الذي يحاول تنفيذ بحث بالقوة الغاشمة في فضاء المفاتيح للعثور على "
"مفتاح يفكّ تشفير الرسالة أن يُنجز عددًا من العمليات يتناسب مع حجم فضاء "
"المفاتيح.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Therefore, a large key space size provides resistance against brute force "
"attacks by rendering them computationally infeasible. <a href=\"#Table "
"1\">Table 1</a> lists the key space sizes of some well-known ciphers.\n"
msgstr ""
"لذلك، يوفر حجم فضاء المفاتيح الكبير مقاومةً ضد هجمات القوة الغاشمة بجعلها "
"غير ممكنة حسابيًا. يُدرج <a href=\"#Table 1\">الجدول 1</a> أحجام فضاء "
"المفاتيح لبعض الشفرات المعروفة.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Table 1: Key space sizes of some symmetric ciphers {#table-1-key-space-"
"sizes-of-some-symmetric-ciphers}"
msgstr ""
"الجدول 1: أحجام فضاء المفاتيح لبعض الشفرات المتماثلة {#table-1-key-space-"
"sizes-of-some-symmetric-ciphers}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<a id=\"Table 1\"></a>\n"
msgstr "<a id=\"Table 1\"></a>\n"

# doq-bootstrap: dropped, JSX/HTML tags differ from English: | Cipher       |
# Key length       | Key space size
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Cipher       | Key length       | Key space size                            |\n"
"|--------------|------------------|-------------------------------------------|\n"
"| Caeser shift | 1                | alphabet-size                             |\n"
"| Vigenere     | n                | alphabet-size$^\\mathrm{n}$                |\n"
"| One-time-pad | plaintext-length | alphabet-size$^\\mathrm{plaintext-length}$ |\n"
"| DES          | 56               | 2$^\\mathrm{56}$                           |\n"
"| AES-128      | 128              | 2$^\\mathrm{128}$                          |\n"
"| AES-192      | 192              | 2$^\\mathrm{192}$                          |\n"
"| AES-256      | 256              | 2$^\\mathrm{256}$                          |\n"
"| ChaCha20     | 256              | 2$^\\mathrm{256}$                          |\n"
"Modern symmetric key encryption schemes largely overcome the limitations of the classical ciphers. They produce ciphertext resistant to <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Analyzing cryptographic systems to identify their weaknesses, vulnerabilities, or hidden information without having access to the secret keys; the ultimate goal is to bypass security measures implemented by the system. Linear cryptanalysis aims to find an approximation to an encryption function, whilst differential cryptanalysis follows a web of different transformations.\">cryptanalysis</DefinitionTooltip> and feature large key space sizes while also being much more practically efficient than an <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"One-time pad. The key is longer than the message to be sent, with each character of the plaintext being added to the key value.\">OTP</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: dropped, JSX/HTML tags differ from English:
# |--------------|------------------|-------------------------
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Block ciphers**: One class of modern ciphers — such as "
"[DES](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Data_Encryption_Standard&oldid=1154751166)"
" and [AES](https://www.nist.gov/publications/development-advanced-"
"encryption-standard) — achieve security by combining the principles of "
"confusion and diffusion [originally introduced by Claude "
"Shannon](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A_Mathematical_Theory_of_Communication#:~:text=%22A%20Mathematical%20Theory%20of%20Communication,the%20generality%20of%20this%20work)."
" We discuss these notions in a setting where encryption schemes work with "
"binary representations of messages:\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Confusion**: Confusion is the characteristic whereby each bit in the "
"ciphertext depends on multiple bits of the secret key. It ensures that a "
"small change in the secret key modifies almost all the bits of the "
"ciphertext, obscuring the relationship between the ciphertext and the secret"
" key.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Confusion**: هي الخاصية التي بموجبها يعتمد كل bit في النص المشفر على عدة "
"bits من المفتاح السري. وهي تضمن أن أي تغيير بسيط في المفتاح السري يعدّل "
"تقريبًا كل bits النص المشفر، مما يُعمّي العلاقة بين النص المشفر والمفتاح "
"السري.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Diffusion**: Diffusion is the characteristic whereby flipping a single bit"
" in the plain text should modify roughly half the bits in the ciphertext and"
" vice versa. Diffusion hides statistical relationships between the plain "
"text and ciphertext. Ciphers with adequate diffusion satisfy the so-called "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Process of spreading the influence of "
"individual elements of the plaintext over a large portion of the ciphertext "
"during encryption. The goal of diffusion is to ensure that a change in a "
"single bit of the plaintext results in changes to multiple bits in the "
"ciphertext.\">*avalanche criterion*</DefinitionTooltip> of cryptography.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Diffusion**: هي الخاصية التي بموجبها يؤدي قلب bit واحد في النص العادي إلى "
"تعديل ما يقارب نصف bits النص المشفر والعكس صحيح. وتُخفي diffusion العلاقات "
"الإحصائية بين النص العادي والنص المشفر. تُحقق الشفرات ذات الـ diffusion "
"الكافية ما يُعرف بـ <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Process of spreading the"
" influence of individual elements of the plaintext over a large portion of "
"the ciphertext during encryption. The goal of diffusion is to ensure that a "
"change in a single bit of the plaintext results in changes to multiple bits "
"in the ciphertext.\">*avalanche criterion*</DefinitionTooltip> في علم "
"التشفير.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Block ciphers implement confusion and diffusion using cryptographic "
"structures known as [substitution-permutation "
"networks](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Substitution%E2%80%93permutation_network&oldid=1098155951)"
" (SPNs) operating on discrete blocks of data. An <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Substitution Permutation Network. A type of block cipher where "
"bits are a) substituted and b) mixed around a number of iterations, during "
"which the key itself is also transformed.\">SPN</DefinitionTooltip> accepts "
"a block of plain text and the secret key as inputs and performs a specified "
"number of "
"[*rounds*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Round_(cryptography)&oldid=1149554107)"
" of transformations to yield a ciphertext block. Each round is composed of "
"alternating mathematical structures known as substitution boxes "
"[(S-boxes)](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=S-box&oldid=1154458964)"
" and permutation boxes "
"[(P-boxes)](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Permutation_box&oldid=1151700196)"
" or equivalent operations.\n"
msgstr ""
"تُطبّق block ciphers الـ confusion والـ diffusion باستخدام بنى تشفيرية تُعرف"
" بـ [substitution-permutation "
"networks](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Substitution%E2%80%93permutation_network&oldid=1098155951)"
" (SPNs) تعمل على كتل بيانات منفصلة. تقبل الـ <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Substitution Permutation Network. A type of block cipher where "
"bits are a) substituted and b) mixed around a number of iterations, during "
"which the key itself is also transformed.\">SPN</DefinitionTooltip> كتلة من "
"النص العادي والمفتاح السري كمدخلات، وتُنفّذ عددًا محددًا من "
"[*rounds*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Round_(cryptography)&oldid=1149554107)"
" من التحويلات لإنتاج كتلة نص مشفر. يتكوّن كل round من بنى رياضية متناوبة "
"تُعرف بصناديق الاستبدال "
"[(S-boxes)](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=S-box&oldid=1154458964)"
" وصناديق التبديل "
"[(P-boxes)](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Permutation_box&oldid=1151700196)"
" أو ما يعادلها من عمليات.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These respectively implement complex nonlinear and linear transformations on"
" the input blocks, leading to [*avalanche "
"effects*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Avalanche_effect&oldid=1148010716)"
" in the ciphertext.\n"
msgstr ""
"تُطبّق هذه البنى على التوالي تحويلات خطية وغير خطية معقدة على كتل المدخلات، "
"مما يؤدي إلى [*avalanche "
"effects*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Avalanche_effect&oldid=1148010716)"
" في النص المشفر.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"SPNs are designed in such a way that increasing the number of <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The number of times a transformation is repeated by an algorithm.\">rounds</DefinitionTooltip> typically increases the security of the cipher. This leads to the notion of [*security margin*](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4878865/).\n"
"**Security margin:** The security margin of a given SPN-based cryptographic cipher is the difference between the number of rounds in the complete implementation of the cipher and the maximum number of rounds that are known to be breakable using the best-known real-world attack.\n"
msgstr ""
"تُصمَّم SPNs بحيث يزيد تكثيف عدد الـ <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The number of times a transformation is repeated by an algorithm.\">rounds</DefinitionTooltip> عادةً من أمان الشفرة. يقودنا هذا إلى مفهوم [*security margin*](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4878865/).\n"
"**Security margin:** هو الفرق بين عدد rounds في التطبيق الكامل للشفرة المبنية على SPN، وأقصى عدد من rounds يُعرف أنه قابل للكسر باستخدام أفضل هجوم معروف في العالم الواقعي.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For instance, currently the best-known faster-than-brute-force attacks "
"against <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Advanced Encryption Standard is a "
"specification for encryption of data, and was established by NIST in 2001. "
"It was originated from the Rijndael ciphers developed by Joan Daemen and "
"Vincent Rijmen, two Belgium cryptographers. It is defined in FIBS 197 & "
"ISO/IEC 18033-3.\">AES-256</DefinitionTooltip> can break up to 9 rounds out "
"of the total 14 rounds in the full cipher when used in the standard mode "
"known as *Electronic Codebook* (ECB) mode. Therefore, [currently the "
"security margin of AES-256 is 5 "
"rounds](https://doi.org/10.13154/tosc.v2019.i2.55-93).\n"
msgstr ""
"على سبيل المثال، أفضل الهجمات الحالية الأسرع من brute-force ضد "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Advanced Encryption Standard is a "
"specification for encryption of data, and was established by NIST in 2001. "
"It was originated from the Rijndael ciphers developed by Joan Daemen and "
"Vincent Rijmen, two Belgium cryptographers. It is defined in FIBS 197 & "
"ISO/IEC 18033-3.\">AES-256</DefinitionTooltip> يمكنها كسر ما يصل إلى 9 "
"rounds من أصل 14 round في الشفرة الكاملة عند استخدامها في الوضع المعياري "
"المعروف بـ *Electronic Codebook* (ECB) mode. لذلك، [security margin الحالي "
"لـ AES-256 هو 5 rounds](https://doi.org/10.13154/tosc.v2019.i2.55-93).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Stream ciphers:** As an alternative to block ciphers, modern cryptologists"
" have also designed practically secure [*stream "
"ciphers*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Stream_cipher&oldid=1143750236)"
" such as "
"[Chacha20](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Salsa20&oldid=1145010249)."
" These ciphers utilize randomness as a fundamental part of their design and "
"operate on pseudorandom <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A stream of random "
"characters used to encrypt plain text. Used in a stream cipher similarly to "
"how a handwritten one-time pad was used.\">*keystreams*</DefinitionTooltip> "
"of bits instead of discrete blocks of data.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Stream ciphers:** كبديل لـ block ciphers، صمّم علماء التشفير الحديثون "
"أيضًا [*stream "
"ciphers*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Stream_cipher&oldid=1143750236)"
" آمنة عمليًا مثل "
"[Chacha20](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Salsa20&oldid=1145010249)."
" تستخدم هذه الشفرات العشوائية كجزء أساسي من تصميمها، وتعمل على "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A stream of random characters used to "
"encrypt plain text. Used in a stream cipher similarly to how a handwritten "
"one-time pad was used.\">*keystreams*</DefinitionTooltip> شبه عشوائية من "
"bits بدلًا من كتل بيانات منفصلة.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Accordingly, stream ciphers combine a secret key and an [initialization "
"vector](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Initialization_vector&oldid=1136156102)"
" (IV) to seed a [pseudorandom random number "
"generator](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Pseudorandom_number_generator&oldid=1153255020)"
" (PRNG) to produce a <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A stream of random "
"characters used to encrypt plain text. Used in a stream cipher similarly to "
"how a handwritten one-time pad was used.\">keystream</DefinitionTooltip> of "
"random bits which are then combined with the given plain text to yield the "
"ciphertext. In this sense, stream ciphers are similar to a "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"One-time pad. The key is longer than the "
"message to be sent, with each character of the plaintext being added to the "
"key value. Early implementations were paper based.\">one-time "
"pad</DefinitionTooltip> (OTP) but feature shorter secret key lengths and "
"reusable keys, which makes them more practical. However, for the same "
"reason, they do not guarantee perfect secrecy, unlike an OTP.\n"
msgstr ""
"وبناءً على ذلك، تجمع stream ciphers بين مفتاح سري و[initialization "
"vector](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Initialization_vector&oldid=1136156102)"
" (IV) لتغذية [pseudorandom random number "
"generator](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Pseudorandom_number_generator&oldid=1153255020)"
" (PRNG) لإنتاج <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A stream of random characters"
" used to encrypt plain text. Used in a stream cipher similarly to how a "
"handwritten one-time pad was used.\">keystream</DefinitionTooltip> من bits "
"عشوائية تُدمج بعد ذلك مع النص العادي للحصول على النص المشفر. بهذا المعنى، "
"تشبه stream ciphers الـ <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"One-time pad. The "
"key is longer than the message to be sent, with each character of the "
"plaintext being added to the key value. Early implementations were paper "
"based.\">one-time pad</DefinitionTooltip> (OTP) لكنها تتميز بأطوال مفاتيح "
"سرية أقصر ومفاتيح قابلة لإعادة الاستخدام، مما يجعلها أكثر عملية. غير أنها "
"لهذا السبب بالذات لا تضمن السرية المطلقة على عكس OTP.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Semantic security**: We conclude this subsection by returning to the "
"notion of semantic security or <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Indistinguishability under chosen-plaintext attack - refers to "
"a hypothetical game of an adversary guessing which of a set of messages was "
"encrypted with a given key. In essence the attack succeeds if there is "
"insufficient complexity/randomness in an encryption algorithm.\">IND-CPA "
"level security</DefinitionTooltip> introduced above. The basic operations "
"implemented by [block "
"ciphers](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Block_cipher_mode_of_operation&oldid=1154901199#cite_note-23)"
" such as S-box and P-box are deterministic. This means that in standard "
"operating modes such as <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Electronic Codebook "
"Mode. A simple encryption mode which works on a block at a time. Given "
"plaintext will always result in the same ciphertext. It does not hide data "
"well.\">ECB</DefinitionTooltip>, a given plain-text key pair always yields "
"the same ciphertext, a state of affairs that is susceptible to chosen-plain-"
"text attacks.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Semantic security**: نختتم هذا القسم بالعودة إلى مفهوم الـ semantic "
"security أو الـ <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Indistinguishability under "
"chosen-plaintext attack - refers to a hypothetical game of an adversary "
"guessing which of a set of messages was encrypted with a given key. In "
"essence the attack succeeds if there is insufficient complexity/randomness "
"in an encryption algorithm.\">IND-CPA level security</DefinitionTooltip> "
"الذي قدّمناه أعلاه. العمليات الأساسية التي تُنفّذها [block "
"ciphers](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Block_cipher_mode_of_operation&oldid=1154901199#cite_note-23)"
" مثل S-box وP-box هي عمليات حتمية. هذا يعني أنه في أوضاع التشغيل المعيارية "
"مثل <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Electronic Codebook Mode. A simple "
"encryption mode which works on a block at a time. Given plaintext will "
"always result in the same ciphertext. It does not hide data "
"well.\">ECB</DefinitionTooltip>، أي زوج من النص العادي والمفتاح يُنتج دائمًا"
" نفس النص المشفر، وهو وضع عرضة لهجمات chosen-plain-text.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To achieve IND-CPA level security, block ciphers need to operate in a mode "
"that utilizes randomness introduced via a pseudorandom <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Initialization Vector. Typically A random, non-predictably "
"selected value used to initialize a cryptographic algorithm. Very similar to"
" a nonce, and somewhat similar to a salt.\">initialization "
"vector</DefinitionTooltip> (IV) with the additional requirement that no two "
"encryption operations use the same key-IV pair. AES supports several modes "
"of operation, such as [cipher block "
"chaining](https://patents.google.com/patent/US4074066A/en) (CBC), which are "
"IND-CPA secure. A similar requirement also holds for stream ciphers whereby "
"the same key-IV pair should not be used to seed the PRNG more than once if "
"IND-CPA is desired.\n"
msgstr ""
"لتحقيق الأمان بمستوى IND-CPA، تحتاج block ciphers إلى العمل في وضع يستخدم "
"العشوائية المُدخَلة عبر <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Initialization "
"Vector. Typically A random, non-predictably selected value used to "
"initialize a cryptographic algorithm. Very similar to a nonce, and somewhat "
"similar to a salt.\">initialization vector</DefinitionTooltip> (IV) شبه "
"عشوائي مع اشتراط إضافي بأن لا تستخدم أي عمليتان تشفير نفس زوج المفتاح-IV. "
"يدعم AES عدة أوضاع تشغيل مثل [cipher block "
"chaining](https://patents.google.com/patent/US4074066A/en) (CBC) التي توفر "
"أمانًا بمستوى IND-CPA. ينطبق متطلب مشابه أيضًا على stream ciphers حيث يجب "
"عدم استخدام نفس زوج المفتاح-IV لتغذية PRNG أكثر من مرة إن كان IND-CPA "
"مطلوبًا.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Popular symmetric key algorithms {#popular-symmetric-key-algorithms}"
msgstr ""
"خوارزميات التشفير بالمفتاح المتماثل الشائعة {#popular-symmetric-key-"
"algorithms}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Having introduced some basic principles of SKC, we now list a few popular "
"symmetric key algorithms to illustrate a variety of the approaches pursued "
"in modern cryptosystems. Modern block ciphers and stream ciphers are both "
"employed in different contexts as illustrated below.\n"
msgstr ""
"بعد أن قدّمنا بعض المبادئ الأساسية لـ SKC، نُدرج الآن بعض خوارزميات المفتاح "
"المتماثل الشائعة لتوضيح تنوع المقاربات المتبعة في أنظمة التشفير الحديثة. "
"كلٌّ من block ciphers وstream ciphers الحديثة تُستخدم في سياقات مختلفة كما "
"يتضح أدناه.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[**Advanced Encryption "
"Standard:**](https://www.nist.gov/publications/development-advanced-"
"encryption-standard) AES, already introduced above, is currently the de "
"facto standard for SKC owing to its security, efficiency, and performance "
"characteristics. AES features fixed key sizes of 128, 192, and 256 bits and "
"uses a multiround <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Substitution Permutation "
"Network. A type of block cipher where bits are a) substituted and b) mixed "
"around a number of iterations, during which the key itself is also "
"transformed.\">substitution-permutation network</DefinitionTooltip> (SPN). "
"AES is known to be resistant to a wide range of cryptanalytic attacks. AES "
"was announced as a Federal Information Processing Standard (FIPS) for "
"symmetric key encryption in the United States in 2001.`\n"
msgstr ""
"[**Advanced Encryption "
"Standard:**](https://www.nist.gov/publications/development-advanced-"
"encryption-standard) AES، الذي قدّمناه أعلاه، هو المعيار الفعلي الحالي لـ "
"SKC نظرًا لخصائصه الأمنية والكفاءة والأداء. يتميز AES بأحجام مفاتيح ثابتة "
"تبلغ 128 و192 و256 bit ويستخدم <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Substitution "
"Permutation Network. A type of block cipher where bits are a) substituted "
"and b) mixed around a number of iterations, during which the key itself is "
"also transformed.\">substitution-permutation network</DefinitionTooltip> "
"(SPN) متعدد الـ rounds. يُعرف AES بمقاومته لمجموعة واسعة من هجمات "
"cryptanalysis. تم الإعلان عن AES كمعيار Federal Information Processing "
"Standard (FIPS) للتشفير بالمفتاح المتماثل في الولايات المتحدة في عام 2001.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[**Data Encryption Standard (DES) and Triple Data Encryption Standard "
"(3DES):**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Data_Encryption_Standard&oldid=1154751166)"
" DES was a block cipher originally invented by Horst Feistel and coworkers "
"at IBM&reg; in the 1970s and employed a SPN with a relatively short 56-bit "
"key. DES was adopted as a <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Federal "
"Information Processing Standards - Standards developed by NIST in the US for"
" computer processing.\">FIPS</DefinitionTooltip> for symmetric key "
"encryption in the United States until the late 1990s when it was shown to be"
" breakable using brute force attacks with specialized hardware due to its "
"small key space size. Subsequently, 3DES was introduced as a replacement and"
" applies the DES algorithm three times with different keys, increasing the "
"key length to 168 bits. Nevertheless, 3DES is largely superseded by AES.\n"
msgstr ""
"[**Data Encryption Standard (DES) and Triple Data Encryption Standard "
"(3DES):**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Data_Encryption_Standard&oldid=1154751166)"
" كان DES block cipher اخترعه في الأصل Horst Feistel وزملاؤه في IBM&reg; في "
"السبعينيات، واستخدم SPN بمفتاح قصير نسبيًا من 56 bit. اعتُمد DES كـ "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Federal Information Processing Standards - "
"Standards developed by NIST in the US for computer "
"processing.\">FIPS</DefinitionTooltip> للتشفير بالمفتاح المتماثل في الولايات"
" المتحدة حتى أواخر التسعينيات حين ثبت إمكانية كسره باستخدام هجمات brute "
"force بأجهزة متخصصة بسبب صغر حجم مساحة مفاتيحه. لاحقًا، جاء 3DES كبديل "
"يُطبّق خوارزمية DES ثلاث مرات بمفاتيح مختلفة مما يرفع طول المفتاح إلى 168 "
"bit. مع ذلك، تم تجاوز 3DES إلى حد بعيد بفضل AES.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[**Blowfish and "
"Twofish:**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Blowfish_(cipher)&oldid=1120053771)"
" Blowfish and its successor, Twofish, are block ciphers proposed by "
"cryptographer Bruce Schneier in the 1990s. Blowfish and Twofish allow "
"variable key lengths of up to 448 bits and 256 bits respectively, offering "
"some flexibility in the tradeoff between security and performance. Unlike "
"AES, they also feature key-dependent <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Substitution box. Maps a set of n-bit inputs to m-bit outputs "
"via a lookup table. Used to add obscurity (confusion) to symmetric key "
"encryption algorithms.\">S-boxes</DefinitionTooltip>. Twofish was one of the"
" finalists in the NIST competition to select the Advanced Encryption "
"Standard but ultimately was not chosen. Both algorithms are currently "
"considered secure.\n"
msgstr ""
"[**Blowfish and "
"Twofish:**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Blowfish_(cipher)&oldid=1120053771)"
" Blowfish وخلفه Twofish هما block ciphers اقترحهما عالم التشفير Bruce "
"Schneier في التسعينيات. يسمح Blowfish وTwofish بأطوال مفاتيح متغيرة تصل إلى "
"448 bit و256 bit على التوالي، مما يوفر مرونة في الموازنة بين الأمان والأداء."
" على عكس AES، يتضمنان أيضًا <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Substitution "
"box. Maps a set of n-bit inputs to m-bit outputs via a lookup table. Used to"
" add obscurity (confusion) to symmetric key encryption "
"algorithms.\">S-boxes</DefinitionTooltip> تعتمد على المفتاح. كان Twofish أحد"
" المتأهلين النهائيين في منافسة NIST لاختيار معيار AES لكنه لم يُختر في نهاية"
" المطاف. كلتا الخوارزميتين تُعتبران حاليًا آمنتين.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[**Rivest Ciphers (RC2, RC4, RC5, and "
"RC6):**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=RC_algorithm&oldid=1072978900)"
" The Rivest Cipher (RC) family of symmetric key algorithms was designed by "
"Ron Rivest starting in the 1980s. RC2 was an early 64-bit block cipher while"
" RC4 was stream cipher widely-used in security protocols related to web-"
"traffic due to its simplicity and speed. Neither is currently considered "
"secure. RC5 and RC6 are SPN based block ciphers designed with customizable "
"block size, key size, and number of rounds. Like Twofish above, RC6 was a "
"finalist in the NIST AES competition and is considered secure.\n"
msgstr ""
"[**Rivest Ciphers (RC2, RC4, RC5, and "
"RC6):**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=RC_algorithm&oldid=1072978900)"
" عائلة Rivest Cipher (RC) من خوارزميات المفتاح المتماثل صمّمها Ron Rivest "
"ابتداءً من الثمانينيات. كان RC2 block cipher مبكرًا من 64 bit، بينما كان RC4"
" stream cipher استُخدم على نطاق واسع في بروتوكولات الأمان المتعلقة بحركة "
"مرور الويب نظرًا لبساطته وسرعته. لا يُعتبر أيٌّ منهما آمنًا حاليًا. RC5 وRC6"
" هما block ciphers مبنيان على SPN وصُمّما بحجم block وحجم مفتاح وعدد rounds "
"قابلة للتخصيص. مثل Twofish أعلاه، كان RC6 متأهلًا نهائيًا في منافسة NIST لـ "
"AES ويُعتبر آمنًا.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[**Salsa20 and "
"ChaCha20:**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Salsa20&oldid=1145010249)"
" Salsa20 and ChaCha20 refer to a related family of stream ciphers designed "
"by cryptographer Daniel Bernstein in the 2000s. Salsa20 is a part of the "
"eSTREAM European Union cryptographic validation project's profile-1 "
"portfolio. ChaCha20, a modification of Salsa20, was designed to increase "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Diffusion is the characteristic whereby "
"flipping a single bit in the plain text should modify roughly half the bits "
"in the ciphertext and vice versa. Diffusion hides statistical relationships "
"between the plain text and ciphertext. Ciphers with adequate diffusion "
"satisfy the so-called avalanche criterion of "
"cryptography.\">diffusion</DefinitionTooltip> characteristics and "
"performance. Currently, ChaCha20 is considered secure and offers better "
"performance in the absence of dedicated AES hardware acceleration. "
"Therefore, ChaCha20 finds use in certain settings such as network protocols "
"like <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Quick UDP Internet Connections. "
"Developed by google for more efficient connections. Now standardized, and "
"used within the HTTP/3 stack amongst other "
"places.\">QUIC</DefinitionTooltip> and mobile devices with ARM-based CPUs.\n"
msgstr ""
"[**Salsa20 and "
"ChaCha20:**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Salsa20&oldid=1145010249)"
" Salsa20 وChaCha20 هما عائلة متعلقة من stream ciphers صمّمها عالم التشفير "
"Daniel Bernstein في العقد الأول من الألفية الثالثة. Salsa20 جزء من محفظة "
"profile-1 لمشروع eSTREAM الأوروبي للتحقق من صحة التشفير. ChaCha20، وهو تعديل"
" على Salsa20، صُمّم لتعزيز خصائص الـ <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Diffusion is the characteristic whereby flipping a single bit "
"in the plain text should modify roughly half the bits in the ciphertext and "
"vice versa. Diffusion hides statistical relationships between the plain text"
" and ciphertext. Ciphers with adequate diffusion satisfy the so-called "
"avalanche criterion of cryptography.\">diffusion</DefinitionTooltip> "
"والأداء. يُعتبر ChaCha20 حاليًا آمنًا ويوفر أداءً أفضل في غياب تسريع AES "
"المخصص في الأجهزة. لذلك يجد ChaCha20 استخدامًا في سياقات معينة مثل "
"بروتوكولات الشبكات كـ <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Quick UDP Internet "
"Connections. Developed by google for more efficient connections. Now "
"standardized, and used within the HTTP/3 stack amongst other "
"places.\">QUIC</DefinitionTooltip> والأجهزة المحمولة ذات المعالجات المبنية "
"على ARM.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Advantages of symmetric key cryptography {#advantages-of-symmetric-key-"
"cryptography}"
msgstr ""
"مزايا التشفير بالمفتاح المتماثل {#advantages-of-symmetric-key-cryptography}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"After outlining the properties of symmetric key cryptosystems and some of "
"the principles that underlie their development, we now list some of the main"
" advantages of [SKC](https://books.google.com/books?id=01vfjgEACAAJ) "
"relative to asymmetric key cryptography. The latter will be discussed in "
"subsequent lessons.\n"
msgstr ""
"بعد أن استعرضنا خصائص أنظمة التشفير بالمفتاح المتماثل وبعض المبادئ التي "
"تُبنى عليها، نُدرج الآن بعضًا من أبرز مزايا "
"[SKC](https://books.google.com/books?id=01vfjgEACAAJ) مقارنةً بالتشفير "
"بالمفتاح غير المتماثل. سنناقش الأخير في الدروس التالية.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Speed and efficiency:** Symmetric key algorithms are more suitable for "
"encrypting large volumes of data or for use in real-time communication "
"scenarios since they are generally faster and less resource intensive than "
"their asymmetric counterparts. SKC algorithms such as AES scale linearly "
"with the size of the plain text and do not involve algebraically intensive "
"mathematical operations. See [Tomoiaga et "
"al.](https://doi.org/10.1109/ICSNC.2010.33) for a detailed review of the "
"performance characteristics of AES.\n"
msgstr ""
"**السرعة والكفاءة:** خوارزميات المفتاح المتماثل أكثر ملاءمة لتشفير كميات "
"كبيرة من البيانات أو للاستخدام في سيناريوهات الاتصال الفوري، إذ إنها بشكل "
"عام أسرع وأقل استهلاكًا للموارد مقارنةً بنظيراتها غير المتماثلة. خوارزميات "
"SKC مثل AES تتناسب خطيًا مع حجم النص العادي ولا تتضمن عمليات رياضية جبرية "
"مكثفة. راجع [Tomoiaga et al.](https://doi.org/10.1109/ICSNC.2010.33) للاطلاع"
" على مراجعة تفصيلية لخصائص أداء AES.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Scalability:** Owing to their relatively low computational overhead, "
"symmetric key algorithms scale well with the number of users and the amount "
"of data being encrypted.\n"
msgstr ""
"**قابلية التوسع:** نظرًا للحمل الحسابي المنخفض نسبيًا، تتوسع خوارزميات "
"المفتاح المتماثل بشكل جيد مع زيادة عدد المستخدمين وحجم البيانات "
"المُشفَّرة.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Simplicity:** Symmetric encryption protocols are often easier to implement"
" and understand compared to asymmetric key approaches, making them "
"attractive for developers and users.\n"
msgstr ""
"**البساطة:** بروتوكولات التشفير المتماثل غالبًا أسهل في التطبيق والفهم "
"مقارنةً بمقاربات المفتاح غير المتماثل، مما يجعلها جذابة للمطورين "
"والمستخدمين.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Challenges and limitations of symmetric key cryptography {#challenges-and-"
"limitations-of-symmetric-key-cryptography}"
msgstr ""
"تحديات وقيود التشفير بالمفتاح المتماثل {#challenges-and-limitations-of-"
"symmetric-key-cryptography}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Despite the advantages, symmetric key cryptography also has some challenges "
"and limitations:\n"
msgstr ""
"على الرغم من المزايا، يواجه التشفير بالمفتاح المتماثل أيضًا بعض التحديات "
"والقيود:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Key distribution and management:** In SKC, both the sender and the "
"receiver of a message must have access to the same key, which must be kept "
"confidential from unauthorized parties. If the key is somehow intercepted or"
" compromised by a third party then the security of the encrypted data is "
"also lost. The secure distribution and management of the secret key is "
"therefore a major challenge. However, the solution to this challenge lies "
"outside of SKC itself.\n"
msgstr ""
"**توزيع المفاتيح وإدارتها:** في SKC، يجب أن يمتلك كلٌّ من المُرسِل "
"والمُستقبِل للرسالة نفس المفتاح الذي يجب الحفاظ على سريته من الأطراف غير "
"المصرّح لها. إن اعتُرض المفتاح أو كُشف بأي طريقة من قِبَل طرف ثالث، فإن أمان"
" البيانات المشفرة يضيع أيضًا. لذا فإن التوزيع الآمن للمفتاح السري وإدارته "
"يُمثّل تحديًا كبيرًا. غير أن الحل لهذا التحدي يقع خارج نطاق SKC نفسها.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Lack of non-repudiation:** [Non-"
"repudiation](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Non-"
"repudiation&oldid=1148337707) refers to the ability to prove that a specific"
" party has sent a message. In SKC, since the same key is used for both "
"encryption and decryption, it is not possible to determine which party has "
"created a particular ciphertext. In contrast, asymmetric key cryptography "
"provides non-repudiation through the use of <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Trace used to verify authenticity, integrity, and origin of "
"digital documents/data; provides a way to ensure object has not been altered"
" and is from the intended sender.\">digital signature</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"
msgstr ""
"**غياب عدم الإنكار:** يشير [Non-"
"repudiation](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Non-"
"repudiation&oldid=1148337707) إلى القدرة على إثبات أن طرفًا معينًا قد أرسل "
"رسالة ما. في SKC، بما أن المفتاح نفسه يُستخدم للتشفير وفك التشفير، لا يمكن "
"تحديد أي طرف أنشأ نصًا مشفرًا معينًا. في المقابل، يوفر التشفير بالمفتاح غير "
"المتماثل عدم الإنكار من خلال استخدام <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Trace "
"used to verify authenticity, integrity, and origin of digital "
"documents/data; provides a way to ensure object has not been altered and is "
"from the intended sender.\">digital signature</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To address these challenges, symmetric key cryptography is often used in "
"combination with asymmetric key cryptography. For instance, one often uses "
"asymmetric key encryption to securely transmit a relatively short shared "
"secret key between sender and receiver. This enables the subsequent use of "
"symmetric key encryption to transmit much larger data and messages "
"efficiently.\n"
msgstr ""
"لمعالجة هذه التحديات، كثيرًا ما يُستخدم التشفير بالمفتاح المتماثل بالتزامن "
"مع التشفير بالمفتاح غير المتماثل. فمثلًا، يُستخدم عادةً التشفير بالمفتاح غير"
" المتماثل لنقل مفتاح سري مشترك قصير نسبيًا بأمان بين المُرسِل والمُستقبِل. "
"هذا يُتيح لاحقًا استخدام التشفير بالمفتاح المتماثل لنقل بيانات ورسائل أكبر "
"بكفاءة أعلى.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum computing and symmetric key encryption: Risks and mitigation "
"{#quantum-computing-and-symmetric-key-encryption-risks-and-mitigation}"
msgstr ""
"الحوسبة الكمومية والتشفير بالمفتاح المتماثل: المخاطر والتخفيف {#quantum-"
"computing-and-symmetric-key-encryption-risks-and-mitigation}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum cryptography offers a promising avenue for risk mitigation in the "
"digital age, with the adoption of quantum-safe products poised to secure our"
" information against the looming threat of quantum computing advancements.\n"
msgstr ""
"يوفر التشفير الكمومي طريقًا واعدًا للتخفيف من المخاطر في العصر الرقمي، مع "
"التوجه نحو اعتماد المنتجات الآمنة كميًا لتأمين معلوماتنا في مواجهة التهديد "
"المتزايد من تطورات الحوسبة الكمومية.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In what follows, we discuss the risks posed by quantum computers to "
"symmetric key encryption schemes introduced in the previous section and "
"outline some potential pathways to mitigating the risks.\n"
msgstr ""
"فيما يلي نتحدث عن المخاطر التي تشكّلها الحواسيب الكمومية على أنظمة التشفير "
"بالمفتاح المتماثل التي قدّمناها في القسم السابق، ونستعرض بعض المسارات "
"المحتملة للتخفيف من هذه المخاطر.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum cryptographic attacks {#quantum-cryptographic-attacks}"
msgstr "هجمات التشفير الكمومية {#quantum-cryptographic-attacks}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are two distinct classes of quantum threats to traditional "
"cryptographic algorithms:\n"
msgstr ""
"هناك فئتان متمايزتان من التهديدات الكمومية للخوارزميات التشفيرية "
"التقليدية:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Quantum brute force attacks**: These refer to situations where the "
"attacker uses a quantum computer to execute a specialized quantum algorithm "
"to conduct a brute force search through the key space of a symmetric cipher."
" The most relevant quantum primitive for enabling this kind of attack is "
"[Grover's algorithm](https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/237814.237866).\n"
msgstr ""
"**Quantum brute force attacks**: تشير إلى مواقف يستخدم فيها المهاجم حاسوبًا "
"كميًا لتنفيذ خوارزمية كمومية متخصصة لإجراء بحث brute force في مساحة مفاتيح "
"شفرة متماثلة. البدائي الكمومي الأكثر أهمية لتمكين هذا النوع من الهجمات هو "
"[Grover's algorithm](https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/237814.237866).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Quantum cryptanalytic attacks**: These refer to situations where quantum "
"computers are deployed to execute cryptanalytic attacks that aim to recover "
"either the secret key or plain text in a more efficient manner than a brute "
"force search. The possibility of executing successful quantum "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Analyzing cryptographic systems to identify "
"their weaknesses, vulnerabilities, or hidden information without having "
"access to the secret keys; the ultimate goal is to bypass security measures "
"implemented by the system. Linear cryptanalysis aims to find an "
"approximation to an encryption function, whilst differential cryptanalysis "
"follows a web of different "
"transformations.\">cryptanalytic</DefinitionTooltip> attacks depends on many"
" factors having to do with the mathematical structure of the cipher being "
"analyzed as well as potential weaknesses in specific implementations.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Quantum cryptanalytic attacks**: تشير إلى مواقف يُنشَر فيها الحواسيب "
"الكمومية لتنفيذ هجمات cryptanalytic تهدف إلى استرداد المفتاح السري أو النص "
"العادي بطريقة أكثر كفاءة من بحث brute force. إمكانية تنفيذ هجمات "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Analyzing cryptographic systems to identify "
"their weaknesses, vulnerabilities, or hidden information without having "
"access to the secret keys; the ultimate goal is to bypass security measures "
"implemented by the system. Linear cryptanalysis aims to find an "
"approximation to an encryption function, whilst differential cryptanalysis "
"follows a web of different "
"transformations.\">cryptanalytic</DefinitionTooltip> كمومية ناجحة تعتمد على "
"عوامل عديدة تتعلق بالبنية الرياضية للشفرة المُحلَّلة وكذلك نقاط ضعف محتملة "
"في تطبيقات بعينها.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Risk mitigation strategies for quantum attacks {#risk-mitigation-strategies-"
"for-quantum-attacks}"
msgstr ""
"استراتيجيات التخفيف من مخاطر الهجمات الكمومية {#risk-mitigation-strategies-"
"for-quantum-attacks}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Before we discuss risk mitigation strategies for quantum attacks, let's "
"introduce the notion of a cryptographic cipher's [security "
"level](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Security_level&oldid=1131789113):\n"
msgstr ""
"قبل أن نتحدث عن استراتيجيات التخفيف من مخاطر الهجمات الكمومية، لنتعرف على "
"مفهوم [مستوى "
"الأمان](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Security_level&oldid=1131789113)"
" للشفرة التشفيرية:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Security level** is a measure of the difficulty of breaking a cipher "
"measured in terms of the number of computational operations that a "
"successful break of the cipher would require.\n"
msgstr ""
"**مستوى الأمان** هو مقياس لمدى صعوبة كسر شفرة ما، يُقاس من حيث عدد العمليات "
"الحسابية التي يتطلبها الكسر الناجح للشفرة.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Typically, the security level is expressed in bits; that is, in general, a "
"cipher offers N-bit security if it requires $\\mathcal{O}(2^{N})$ operations"
" to break it. On classical computers, assuming a symmetric cipher is "
"otherwise cryptographically secure, the security level is roughly synonymous"
" with the key length.\n"
msgstr ""
"عادةً، يُعبَّر عن مستوى الأمان بالـ bits؛ أي بشكل عام، توفر الشفرة أمانًا بـ"
" N bit إذا تطلبت $\\mathcal{O}(2^{N})$ عملية لكسرها. على الحواسيب "
"الكلاسيكية، بافتراض أن الشفرة المتماثلة آمنة من الناحية التشفيرية في جوانبها"
" الأخرى، يكون مستوى الأمان مرادفًا تقريبًا لطول المفتاح.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For instance, the security level of AES-128, which features a 128-bit key, "
"is generally considered to be 128 bits because it would require on the order"
" of 2$^{128}$ operations for an attacker employing a classical computer to "
"try out all possible 128-bit keys in the key space.\n"
msgstr ""
"على سبيل المثال، يُعتبر مستوى الأمان لـ AES-128 الذي يتميز بمفتاح 128 bit "
"عمومًا 128 bit، لأنه سيتطلب من المهاجم الذي يستخدم حاسوبًا كلاسيكيًا ما "
"يقارب 2$^{128}$ عملية لتجربة جميع المفاتيح الممكنة من 128 bit في مساحة "
"المفاتيح.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Brute force attacks and mitigation {#brute-force-attacks-and-mitigation}"
msgstr "هجمات brute force والتخفيف منها {#brute-force-attacks-and-mitigation}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Quantum brute force attack risk:** A [quantum brute force "
"attack](https://inria.hal.science/hal-01237242) changes the above assessment"
" because <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Grover's Algorithm is a quantum "
"algorithm for searching through unstructured data. Whilst a classical "
"algorithm may take N/2 steps to search in N items, with Grover's algorithm "
"this is reduced to $sqrt(N)$ .\">Grover's algorithm</DefinitionTooltip> "
"enables an attacker with a suitable quantum computer to search the key space"
" of a cipher <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Quadratically faster refers to "
"a speedup that occurs in relation to the square of the number of values, for"
" example a search, when compared to a simple linear inspection of each "
"value.\">quadratically faster</DefinitionTooltip> than any classical "
"computer.\n"
msgstr ""
"**مخاطر هجوم brute force الكمومي:** يغيّر [هجوم brute force "
"الكمومي](https://inria.hal.science/hal-01237242) هذا التقييم لأن "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Grover's Algorithm is a quantum algorithm "
"for searching through unstructured data. Whilst a classical algorithm may "
"take N/2 steps to search in N items, with Grover's algorithm this is reduced"
" to $sqrt(N)$ .\">Grover's algorithm</DefinitionTooltip> يُمكّن المهاجم الذي"
" يمتلك حاسوبًا كميًا مناسبًا من البحث في مساحة مفاتيح الشفرة بسرعة "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Quadratically faster refers to a speedup "
"that occurs in relation to the square of the number of values, for example a"
" search, when compared to a simple linear inspection of each "
"value.\">تربيعية أسرع</DefinitionTooltip> من أي حاسوب كلاسيكي.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For instance, the same brute force attack on AES-128 with Grover's algorithm"
" could potentially be achieved with just 2$^{64}$ operations. Therefore the "
"security level of AES-128 is reduced from 128 bits to 64 bits when faced "
"with a quantum adversary running Grover search. Since computational power "
"has traditionally grown exponentially with time, currently a security level "
"of 64 bits is considered insecure, which means that once sufficiently "
"capable quantum computers are realized, AES-128 will have to be abandoned.\n"
msgstr ""
"على سبيل المثال، يمكن تحقيق نفس هجوم brute force على AES-128 باستخدام "
"Grover's algorithm بـ 2$^{64}$ عملية فقط. لذلك ينخفض مستوى الأمان لـ AES-128"
" من 128 bit إلى 64 bit في مواجهة خصم كمومي يُشغّل Grover search. بما أن "
"القدرة الحسابية نمت تاريخيًا بشكل أسّي مع الوقت، يُعتبر مستوى الأمان البالغ "
"64 bit غير آمن حاليًا، مما يعني أنه بمجرد تحقق حواسيب كمومية كافية القدرة، "
"سيتعين التخلي عن AES-128.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The same kind of calculation applies to other symmetric block or stream "
"ciphers whereby the security level for a given key length is effectively "
"halved by Grover's algorithm.\n"
msgstr ""
"ينطبق نفس النوع من الحسابات على block ciphers أو stream ciphers المتماثلة "
"الأخرى، حيث ينخفض مستوى الأمان لطول مفتاح معين فعليًا إلى النصف بفعل "
"Grover's algorithm.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Quantum brute force attack risk mitigation:** The above considerations "
"imply that an obvious way to resist quantum brute force attacks is to at "
"least [double the minimum key lengths used for symmetric key "
"encryption](https://inria.hal.science/hal-01237242).\n"
msgstr ""
"**التخفيف من مخاطر هجوم brute force الكمومي:** تُلمّح الاعتبارات أعلاه إلى "
"أن طريقة واضحة لمقاومة هجمات brute force الكمومية هي على الأقل [مضاعفة الحد "
"الأدنى لأطوال المفاتيح المستخدمة للتشفير بالمفتاح "
"المتماثل](https://inria.hal.science/hal-01237242).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Therefore, to ensure 128-bit security with regard to quantum brute force "
"attacks, one would simply use ciphers such as AES-256 or ChaCha20 that "
"employ 256-bit keys. This is considered secure because even with quantum "
"computers, performing 2$^{128}$ operations to break ciphers is infeasible in"
" the foreseeable future.\n"
msgstr ""
"لذلك، لضمان أمان بمستوى 128 bit في مواجهة هجمات brute force الكمومية، يكفي "
"استخدام شفرات مثل AES-256 أو ChaCha20 التي تستخدم مفاتيح 256 bit. يُعتبر هذا"
" آمنًا لأنه حتى مع الحواسيب الكمومية، فإن تنفيذ 2$^{128}$ عملية لكسر الشفرات"
" غير ممكن عمليًا في المستقبل المنظور.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"While theoretically simple, this proposed solution of doubling key sizes is "
"not without costs, as longer key sizes imply additional computational cost "
"for routine encryption-decryption tasks, along with slower performance, more"
" memory requirement, and additional energy use.\n"
msgstr ""
"على الرغم من بساطته النظرية، فإن الحل المقترح بمضاعفة أحجام المفاتيح ليس "
"بدون تكاليف، إذ تعني أحجام المفاتيح الأكبر تكاليف حسابية إضافية لمهام "
"التشفير وفك التشفير الاعتيادية، إلى جانب أداء أبطأ ومتطلبات ذاكرة أعلى "
"واستهلاك طاقة إضافي.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Cryptanalytic attacks and mitigation {#cryptanalytic-attacks-and-mitigation}"
msgstr ""
"هجمات cryptanalytic والتخفيف منها {#cryptanalytic-attacks-and-mitigation}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Quantum cryptanalytic attacks risk:** The risk to symmetric key "
"cryptosystems posed by quantum cryptanalytic attacks is currently being "
"[actively researched by "
"cryptographers](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0045790622003743)."
" The combination of classical and quantum computing potentially expands the "
"array of tools available to attackers to probe weaknesses in the "
"mathematical structure of ciphers, and a wide range of new "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Quantum Cryptoanalytic attack. Refers to "
"situations where quantum computers are deployed to execute cryptanalytic "
"attacks that aim to recover either the secret key or plain text in a more "
"efficient manner than a brute force search.\">quantum cryptanalytic "
"attacks</DefinitionTooltip> are currently being proposed. These include "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Quantization is the process of mapping a "
"values from a large set of values, to a smaller set of values. For example "
"16 bit audio sampling maps from a continuous frequency value into a value "
"represented in 16 bits, In quantum computing it can convert a floating point"
" number into a quantum-entangled qbit. This can then be used in search "
"algorithms such as Grover's algorithm.\">quantizations</DefinitionTooltip> "
"of known classical techniques such as [linear and differential "
"cryptanalysis](https://inria.hal.science/hal-01237242) as well as new attack"
" modes with no classical counterparts.\n"
msgstr ""
"**مخاطر هجمات cryptanalytic الكمومية:** المخاطر التي تتعرض لها أنظمة التشفير"
" بالمفتاح المتماثل من هجمات cryptanalytic كمومية يجري [بحثها بنشاط حاليًا من"
" قِبَل علماء "
"التشفير](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0045790622003743)."
" الجمع بين الحوسبة الكلاسيكية والكمومية يوسّع محتملًا مجموعة الأدوات المتاحة"
" للمهاجمين للتحقيق في نقاط ضعف البنية الرياضية للشفرات، ويجري حاليًا اقتراح "
"مجموعة واسعة من <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Quantum Cryptoanalytic "
"attack. Refers to situations where quantum computers are deployed to execute"
" cryptanalytic attacks that aim to recover either the secret key or plain "
"text in a more efficient manner than a brute force search.\">هجمات "
"cryptanalytic كمومية</DefinitionTooltip> جديدة. تشمل هذه <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Quantization is the process of mapping a values from a large "
"set of values, to a smaller set of values. For example 16 bit audio sampling"
" maps from a continuous frequency value into a value represented in 16 bits,"
" In quantum computing it can convert a floating point number into a quantum-"
"entangled qbit. This can then be used in search algorithms such as Grover's "
"algorithm.\">quantizations</DefinitionTooltip> لتقنيات كلاسيكية معروفة مثل "
"[linear and differential "
"cryptanalysis](https://inria.hal.science/hal-01237242) وكذلك أوضاع هجوم "
"جديدة ليس لها نظير كلاسيكي.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A [recent quantum cryptanalytic study of the Advanced Encryption Standard "
"(AES)](https://doi.org/10.13154/tosc.v2019.i2.55-93) found that the cipher "
"remained resistant to various known <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Quantum "
"Cryptoanalytic attack. Refers to situations where quantum computers are "
"deployed to execute cryptanalytic attacks that aim to recover either the "
"secret key or plain text in a more efficient manner than a brute force "
"search.\">quantum cryptanalytic attacks</DefinitionTooltip> and continued to"
" exhibit an adequate post-quantum <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A measure "
"of how much better we need to get at analyzing a cipher to break "
"it.\">security margin</DefinitionTooltip>. However, some studies have found "
"that various symmetric ciphers considered classically secure are easily "
"compromised by so-called [*quantum chosen plain text "
"attack*](https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-56617-7_3). Therefore, new "
"primitives for symmetric key encryption designed specifically for the post-"
"quantum era have also been proposed.\n"
msgstr ""
"وجدت [دراسة حديثة لـ cryptanalysis الكمومي على "
"AES](https://doi.org/10.13154/tosc.v2019.i2.55-93) أن الشفرة ظلت مقاومةً "
"لمختلف <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Quantum Cryptoanalytic attack. Refers"
" to situations where quantum computers are deployed to execute cryptanalytic"
" attacks that aim to recover either the secret key or plain text in a more "
"efficient manner than a brute force search.\">هجمات cryptanalysis "
"الكمومية</DefinitionTooltip> المعروفة واستمرت في إظهار <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"A measure of how much better we need to get at analyzing a "
"cipher to break it.\">security margin</DefinitionTooltip> كافٍ بعد الكم. غير"
" أن بعض الدراسات وجدت أن شفرات متماثلة متعددة تُعتبر آمنة كلاسيكيًا يمكن "
"كسرها بسهولة عبر ما يُعرف بـ [*quantum chosen plain text "
"attack*](https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-56617-7_3). لذلك، اقتُرحت أيضًا "
"بدائل جديدة للتشفير بالمفتاح المتماثل مصمَّمة خصيصًا لعصر ما بعد الكم.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Quantum cryptanalytic attacks risk mitigation:** Given that quantum "
"cryptanalysis as a discipline is in its infancy, it may be the case that "
"post-quantum symmetric cryptography will undergo rapid evolution as new "
"quantum cryptanalytic attacks arise and as new ciphers resistant to them are"
" proposed and evaluated. Therefore, the best strategy to mitigate the risk "
"of quantum cryptanalytic attacks in the foreseeable future is "
"[*cryptographic "
"agility*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Cryptographic_agility&oldid=1155073704)"
" (or crypto-agility). Crypto-agility refers to the ability of an information"
" system to quickly and easily adopt alternative cryptographic primitives "
"without disruptive changes to the system infrastructure.\n"
msgstr ""
"**التخفيف من مخاطر هجمات cryptanalytic الكمومية:** بالنظر إلى أن "
"cryptanalysis الكمومي كتخصص لا يزال في مهده، قد يشهد التشفير بالمفتاح "
"المتماثل بعد الكم تطورًا سريعًا مع ظهور هجمات cryptanalytic كمومية جديدة "
"واقتراح شفرات جديدة مقاومة لها وتقييمها. لذلك، أفضل استراتيجية للتخفيف من "
"مخاطر هجمات cryptanalytic الكمومية في المستقبل المنظور هي [*cryptographic "
"agility*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Cryptographic_agility&oldid=1155073704)"
" (أو crypto-agility). تشير crypto-agility إلى قدرة نظام المعلومات على اعتماد"
" بدائل تشفيرية بسرعة وسهولة دون إجراء تغييرات مُخلِّة في البنية التحتية "
"للنظام.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Crypto-agility requires the ability to replace obsolete algorithms used for "
"encryption, decryption, digital signatures, or other cryptographic functions"
" with minimal effort and disruption. Crypto-agile systems will be well "
"positioned to manage the transition to post-quantum symmetric key "
"cryptography.\n"
msgstr ""
"تتطلب crypto-agility القدرة على استبدال الخوارزميات القديمة المستخدمة "
"للتشفير أو فك التشفير أو التوقيعات الرقمية أو غيرها من الوظائف التشفيرية "
"بأدنى جهد وتعطيل. ستكون الأنظمة المتمتعة بـ crypto-agility في وضع جيد لإدارة"
" الانتقال إلى التشفير بالمفتاح المتماثل بعد الكم.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Summary {#summary}"
msgstr "ملخص {#summary}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Symmetric key cryptography provides robust and efficient solutions for "
"securing digital information. The simplicity of using the same key for both "
"encryption and decryption enables high performance and scalability, making "
"SKC suitable for a wide range of applications.\n"
msgstr ""
"يوفر التشفير بالمفتاح المتماثل حلولًا قوية وفعّالة لتأمين المعلومات الرقمية."
" بساطة استخدام نفس المفتاح للتشفير وفك التشفير تُتيح أداءً عاليًا وقابلية "
"توسع، مما يجعل SKC مناسبًا لمجموعة واسعة من التطبيقات.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The security of SKC relies on algorithmic resistance to cryptographic "
"attacks as well as proper secret key management. Modern symmetric key "
"cryptosystems combine the principles of <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Confusion is the characteristic whereby each bit in the "
"ciphertext depends on multiple bits of the secret key. It ensures that a "
"small change in the secret key modifies almost all the bits of the "
"ciphertext, obscuring the relationship between the ciphertext and the secret"
" key.\">confusion</DefinitionTooltip>, diffusion, and randomness, in "
"conjunction with adequate key sizes, to achieve <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"With only the ciphertext, and any relevant public information "
"(such as public key for asymmetric cryptography), and adversary cannot "
"retrieve even partial information from the plaintext.\">semantic "
"security</DefinitionTooltip>. Secret key management, while crucial, cannot "
"be achieved with SKC alone.\n"
msgstr ""
"يعتمد أمان SKC على مقاومة الخوارزميات للهجمات التشفيرية وعلى الإدارة السليمة"
" للمفتاح السري. تجمع أنظمة التشفير بالمفتاح المتماثل الحديثة بين مبادئ "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Confusion is the characteristic whereby each"
" bit in the ciphertext depends on multiple bits of the secret key. It "
"ensures that a small change in the secret key modifies almost all the bits "
"of the ciphertext, obscuring the relationship between the ciphertext and the"
" secret key.\">confusion</DefinitionTooltip>، وdiffusion، والعشوائية، جنبًا "
"إلى جنب مع أحجام مفاتيح كافية، لتحقيق <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"With "
"only the ciphertext, and any relevant public information (such as public key"
" for asymmetric cryptography), and adversary cannot retrieve even partial "
"information from the plaintext.\">semantic security</DefinitionTooltip>. "
"إدارة المفاتيح السرية، رغم أهميتها البالغة، لا يمكن تحقيقها بـ SKC وحدها.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Understanding the properties and limitations of SKC will enable developers "
"to design, implement, and deploy secure information technology solutions "
"using approaches included longer key sizes as needed, and the use of new "
"algorithms.\n"
msgstr ""
"فهم خصائص وقيود SKC سيُمكّن المطورين من تصميم وتطبيق ونشر حلول تقنية "
"معلوماتية آمنة باستخدام مقاربات تشمل أطوال مفاتيح أكبر عند الحاجة، واستخدام "
"خوارزميات جديدة.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The advancement of quantum computing and quantum learning introduces a new "
"dimension to symmetric key cryptography. Quantum computers have the "
"potential to unravel the security provided by classical symmetric key "
"algorithms, prompting the need for quantum-resistant cryptographic "
"approaches to ensure data privacy and protection in the face of evolving "
"technological landscapes.\n"
msgstr ""
